From ebaaa3028a0b29570ab8c97b62a95f15142d61e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: a52q camera integration <jarda.kotesovec@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 12:09:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] ipa: simple: Add contrast-detect autofocus

Port of the Pixel 4a libcamera-softisp-af.patch (itself a port of the
tui/libcamera millicam AF branch to 0.7.2): a green-channel sharpness
statistic over the central 3x3 of a 5x5 grid in the CPU stats, lens
controls plumbed from the IPA through the software ISP to the sensor's
CameraLens, and a coarse-to-fine sweep with parabolic peak, focus-loss
monitor and warm re-focus in an Af algorithm (AfMode, AfTrigger,
LensPosition 0..100, AfState metadata).

Changes against the Pixel 4a version:

- The brightness / AE enable / manual exposure controls of that patch
  are not carried: they reuse standard control ids with non-standard
  ranges (Brightness 0..2, ExposureValue as an exposure fraction).
- LensPosition 0..100 maps onto [focus_min, focus_max] (the offset was
  missing), and the new optional 'lensRange' tuning key restricts it to
  the module's calibrated infinity..macro codes.
- Without a lens the algorithm does nothing, and the IPA only emits a
  lens position when the Af algorithm computed one, so a lens is never
  parked at code 0 by a tuning file without Af.
- The lens position is applied whether or not the pipeline has a frame
  start event (the Pixel version only moved it without one).
- Only cameras whose tuning file lists 'Af' run it.
